direction: down

title: |md
  ## kTLS — TLS in the kernel
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

setup: "Setup phase (userspace)" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  s_body: |md
    - App opens TCP connection
    - App does TLS handshake in userspace
    - (OpenSSL, GnuTLS, BoringSSL, ...)
    - App calls setsockopt(TLS_TX/TLS_RX,
    - crypto_info) — passes keys to kernel
    - Kernel takes over encrypt/decrypt
  |
}

datapath: "Data path (kernel)" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  d_body: |md
    - Send: app writes plaintext;
    - kernel encrypts in-place; sends
    - Recv: kernel decrypts;
    - app reads plaintext

    Benefits:
    - sendfile() over TLS (zero-copy:
    - file → encrypted → wire)
    - splice() / vmsplice() compatible
    - No userspace crypto roundtrip
  |
}

hw: "Hardware offload" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  h_body: |md
    - Some NICs (Mellanox, Chelsio)
    - can offload AES-GCM encryption
    - With kTLS, kernel passes keys to NIC
    - NIC encrypts/decrypts inline
    - CPU touches only plaintext
    - NIC support: NETIF_F_HW_TLS_TX / RX
  |
}

setup -> datapath -> hw
